Package: edaphos
Title: Digital Soil Mapping with Causal, Physics-Informed and Generative Methods
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R:
    person("Hugo", "Rodrigues", , "rodrigues.machado.hugo@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8070-8126"))
Description: Digital soil mapping methods beyond regression trees,
    organised as ten pillars: causal inference with backdoor
    adjustment on pedogenetic directed acyclic graphs, instrumental
    variables and sensitivity analysis (Cinelli and Hazlett, 2020,
    <doi:10.1111/rssb.12348>); physics-informed learning with a
    pedogenetic ordinary differential equation and a differentiable
    neural ordinary differential equation; four-dimensional pedometry
    with stacked convolutional long short-term memory networks and an
    ensemble Kalman filter; foundation models via 'SimCLR' and 'MoCo'
    contrastive pre-training on raster patches; active learning with
    hybrid uncertainty and diversity policies; quantum machine
    learning with a state-vector feature-map simulator and quantum
    kernel ridge regression; Bayesian hierarchical spatial models with
    a Gibbs sampler ('RcppArmadillo' backend); neural operators
    ('DeepONet' and the Fourier neural operator) over depth-function
    space; denoising diffusion probabilistic models for soil-property
    maps; and graph attention networks (Velickovic and others, 2018,
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1710.10903>). A shared calibration class scores
    every method with the same uncertainty diagnostics. A synthesised
    Cerrado dataset is bundled so vignettes run offline. See McBratney,
    Mendonca Santos and Minasny (2003, <doi:10.1016/S0016-7061(03)00223-4>)
    for the digital soil mapping framework.
